+# CI-02 Task Log
+
+- Date: 2026-03-08
+- Scope: frontend CI-equivalent Vitest timeout recovery
+
+## Reproduction
+- Ran `cd backend && npm run test:all`
+  - Result: sandbox-only failure `listen EPERM 0.0.0.0` in `backend/src/app.test.js`
+- Ran `cd frontend && npm run test`
+  - Result: 3 failing timeout tests in full suite
+    - `src/app/customs-declarations/create/page.test.tsx`
+    - `src/app/customs-declarations/[id]/edit/page.test.tsx`
+    - `src/app/dashboard/settings/ports/page.test.tsx`
+
+## Root Cause Investigation
+- Ran the 3 failing frontend files individually; all passed.
+- Ran the same suite with a larger timeout to confirm the failures were time-budget related, not behavior regressions.
+- Confirmed coverage instrumentation further increases runtime for the same high-interaction page tests.
+
+## Fix
+- Updated `frontend/vitest.config.ts` to set `testTimeout: 20000`.
+- Kept production code unchanged.
+
+## Verification
+- `cd frontend && npm run test` -> pass (`101 files / 313 tests`)
+- `cd frontend && npm run test:coverage` -> pass (`101 files / 313 tests`)
+
+## Notes
+- An intermediate attempt ran `test` and `test:coverage` in parallel and produced artificial slowdowns; those results were discarded.
+- Backend `EPERM` reproduction is environment-specific to this sandbox and was not treated as the CI root cause for this task.
