+# CI-02 Result
+
+## Outcome
+- Fixed the reproducible frontend CI-equivalent failure by relaxing Vitest's default timeout budget for full-suite and coverage runs.
+
+## Root Cause
+- The failing tests were not functionally broken.
+- `jsdom + user-event` page-interaction tests exceeded Vitest's default `5s` timeout when run as part of the full suite, and became even slower with coverage instrumentation.
+
+## Files Changed
+- `frontend/vitest.config.ts`
+- checkpoint artifacts:
+  - `PLAN.md`
+  - `TASKS.md`
+  - `METRICS.md`
+  - `RISKS.md`
+  - `frontend/PLAN.md`
+  - `frontend/TASKS.md`
+  - `frontend/METRICS.md`
+  - `frontend/RISKS.md`
+
+## Verification Evidence
+- `cd frontend && npm run test`
+  - Pass: `101 files / 313 tests`
+- `cd frontend && npm run test:coverage`
+  - Pass: `101 files / 313 tests`
+  - Coverage: `73.28%` statements / `80.2%` branches / `67.45%` functions / `73.28%` lines
+
+## Residual Notes
+- `cd backend && npm run test:all` still hits `listen EPERM 0.0.0.0` in this sandbox because the test opens a socket; this was not the failing frontend CI gate addressed here.
